# Plugin pages

Server plugins render pages at `<base><mount>/-/<name>/` (`server.pages`, factory `{ handle, page }`). `createServer` in `@svartz/core` builds the handle and `svartzPage`; the route `src/routes/[...slug]/-/[...page]/` calls `svartzPage` from its server `load` and renders `SvartzPluginPage`.

- Never add a branch, `{#if}` or prop-driven markup for plugin pages to `SvartzVaultPage` or `SvartzRuntimePage`. Every block adds hydration markers to every prerendered note, and the contract is that vaults without plugin pages prerender unchanged. Plugin page rendering belongs in `SvartzPluginPage`.
- Prove "unchanged output" by building the same vault on the base commit and the branch and diffing after normalizing build-specific values: `_app/immutable` names, SvelteKit's version and `__sveltekit_<hash>`, `svelte-<hash>` classes and `<!--hash-->` ids (they depend on the checkout path), CSP script hashes, and timestamps. Give both vault copies the same mtimes; equal dates order notes by mtime. The new route adds one shared `modulepreload` link; nothing else may differ.
- The page route must keep `prerender = false`; adapter-static without a `fallback` refuses it, so `svartz init` skips it in static hosts.
- Pages are GET-only. Forms post to the plugin's `/_svartz/<id>/` routes and redirect back with a 303.
